---
description: Odoo backend/frontend development conventions (Python/ORM, views, security, OWL)
globs: **/*.py, **/*.xml, **/*.js, **/*.csv, **/__manifest__.py
alwaysApply: false
---

When writing or reviewing Odoo module code, follow the senior developer playbook for the target version:

- Load `@knowledge/odoo-19/developer/SKILL.md` (or `odoo-18` / `odoo-17`) and its `references/` — `orm.md`, `models-fields.md`, `views-owl.md`, `security.md`, `performance-testing.md`, and the per-version changes file (`v19-changes.md` / `v18-changes.md` / `v17-changes.md`).
- Models: `_description` always, recordset methods, `@api.model_create_multi`, complete `@api.depends`, `store=True` only when searched/grouped/sorted.
- DB-side search/group (`search_fetch`, `_read_group`, domains); no `search`/`browse` in loops; no `cr.commit()`; parameterized `odoo.tools.SQL` only.
- Security with every model: `ir.model.access.csv`, record rules, group-gated fields/menus/buttons; `sudo()` only narrowly and commented.
- **Match the version's syntax:** list root `<tree>` (17) vs `<list>` (18/19); `oe_chatter` div (17) vs `<chatter/>` (18/19); `check_access_rights`/`_rule` (17) vs `check_access`/`has_access` (18/19); `groups_id` (17/18) vs `group_ids` (19); `_sql_constraints` (17/18) vs declarative `models.Constraint` (19). No `attrs`/`states` (removed in 17). Owl 2; `t-out` not `t-raw`.
- Tests: `TransactionCase`, `HttpCase`/tours, `Form`; QUnit (17) or Hoot (18/19) for JS.

Never edit core; extend via `_inherit`/xpath. Never invent an API — verify against the version's docs.
